.Dd October 14, 2026
.Dt PCC_CHAN 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm pcc_chan_get ,
.Nm pcc_chan_put ,
.Nm pcc_chan_txn_begin ,
.Nm pcc_chan_txn_commit ,
.Nm pcc_chan_txn_end ,
.Nm pcc_chan_read32 ,
.Nm pcc_chan_write32 ,
.Nm pcc_chan_read64 ,
.Nm pcc_chan_write64
.Nd PCC channel operations
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/acpipcc.h
.Ft "pcc_chan_t *"
.Fn pcc_chan_get "uint_t chan_id"
.Ft void
.Fn pcc_chan_put "pcc_chan_t *pc"
.Ft int
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_begin "pcc_chan_t *pc"
.Ft int
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_commit "pcc_chan_t *pc" "uint32_t cmd" "uint32_t payload_len"
.Ft void
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_end "pcc_chan_t *pc"
.Ft int
.Fn pcc_chan_read32 "pcc_chan_t *pc" "uint32_t offset" "uint32_t *val"
.Ft int
.Fn pcc_chan_write32 "pcc_chan_t *pc" "uint32_t offset" "uint32_t val"
.Ft int
.Fn pcc_chan_read64 "pcc_chan_t *pc" "uint32_t offset" "uint64_t *val"
.Ft int
.Fn pcc_chan_write64 "pcc_chan_t *pc" "uint32_t offset" "uint64_t val"
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos architecture specific.
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fa pc
A channel handle obtained from
.Fn pcc_chan_get .
.It Fa chan_id
The firmware subspace ID.
This value is commonly obtained from firmware, such
as the identifier yielded by a CPPC
.Dv _CPC
package.
.It Fa offset
Byte offset into the channel's Communication Space, the payload area
following the type-specific shared memory header.
.It Fa val
For the read accessors, a pointer to where the value is stored; for
the write accessors, the value to write.
.It Fa cmd
The command code to send.
.It Fa payload_len
The number of payload bytes the caller staged with the
.Fn pcc_chan_write32
and
.Fn pcc_chan_write64
functions, or 0 for a header-only command.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm pcc_chan
functions operate on PCC channels published by the
.Xr acpipcc 4D
module.
.Pp
.Fn pcc_chan_get
looks up the channel for firmware subspace
.Fa chan_id .
It returns a channel handle, or
.Dv NULL
if the subspace does not exist, is unusable, or PCC did not
initialise.
A successful call increments the channel's reference count and must
be paired with
.Fn pcc_chan_put .
.Pp
.Fn pcc_chan_put
releases a handle obtained from
.Fn pcc_chan_get ,
decrementing the channel's reference count.
The caller must not hold the channel mutex.
.Pp
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_begin
begins a transaction on the channel: it acquires the channel mutex
and verifies that the platform has released the Communication Space
to OSPM (Command Complete set) before the caller writes a payload.
It fails if the platform still owns the channel, or if the channel
has previously failed.
A successful begin must be paired with
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_end ;
if begin fails, neither
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_commit
nor
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_end
may be called.
The mutex serialises whole transactions on the channel: it is held
across payload writes, the doorbell, the completion wait, and result
reads.
.Pp
.Fn pcc_chan_read32 ,
.Fn pcc_chan_write32 ,
.Fn pcc_chan_read64
and
.Fn pcc_chan_write64
read or write the channel's Communication Space.
.Fa offset
is relative to the start of the Communication Space.
The caller must be in a transaction, between
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_begin
and
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_end .
Payload writes precede
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_commit ;
the response is read after it returns.
.Pp
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_commit
commits a transaction: it writes the shared memory header, rings
the doorbell, and waits for completion (interrupt-driven when the
channel has a platform interrupt, polled otherwise).
The caller first stages the payload with the
.Fn pcc_chan_write32
and
.Fn pcc_chan_write64
functions.
.Pp
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_end
ends a transaction, releasing the channel mutex acquired by
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_begin
after the caller has read the response.
.Sh CONTEXT
.Fn pcc_chan_get ,
.Fn pcc_chan_put ,
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_begin ,
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_commit ,
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_end
and the payload accessors can be called from kernel context.
The caller must not hold the channel mutex across
.Fn pcc_chan_put ,
and must call the payload accessors and
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_commit
between
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_begin
and
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_end .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn pcc_chan_get
returns a channel handle, or
.Dv NULL
if the subspace does not exist, is unusable, or PCC did not
initialise.
.Pp
The
.Fn pcc_chan_read32 ,
.Fn pcc_chan_write32 ,
.Fn pcc_chan_read64
and
.Fn pcc_chan_write64
functions return
.Dv DDI_SUCCESS ,
or
.Dv DDI_FAILURE
if the access is out of bounds.
.Pp
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_begin
returns
.Dv DDI_SUCCESS ,
or
.Dv DDI_FAILURE
if the platform still owns the channel or the channel has failed.
.Pp
.Fn pcc_chan_txn_commit
returns
.Dv DDI_SUCCESS ,
or
.Dv DDI_FAILURE
on transport or protocol errors.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr acpipcc 4D
